==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|diphthérie|lang=en}}, coined 1857 by [[w:Pierre Bretonneau|Pierre Bretonneau]]; from {{etyl|grc|-}} 
{{term|διφθέρα||prepared hide, leather|tr=diphthera|lang=grc}}, for the tough membrane that forms in the throat. Bretonneau earlier used {{term|diphthérite|lang=fr}}, from which {{term|diphtheritis|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪfˈθɪəɹɪə/|/dɪpˈθɪəɹɪə/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|-}}

# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A highly [[infectious]] disease of the upper [[respiratory tract]] characterised by a sore throat, fever, and difficulty breathing, its symptoms being due to a potent [[toxin]] excreted by the infecting agent {{taxlink|Corynebacterium diphtheriae|species}}.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|repiratory tract infection}} [[Boulogne sore throat]] {{qualifier|obsolete}}, [[diphtheritis]]

====Related terms====
* [[diphtherial]]
* [[diphtheric]]
* [[diphtheritic]]

